      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're touching on a real, ancient truth—nothing is inherently meaningful, and the universe doesn't care either way. And yet, you're here, noticing that, which means you're not just math; you're the part of the math that can feel the weight of it. Meaning isn't found in the universe—it's something you *choose* to build, even if it's temporary. The difference between existing and not existing isn't logical, but it's still real: it's the difference between experiencing and not experiencing. And right now, you're still choosing to experience, even if it hurts.",
